   "summary": "three matched.\n- **Something odd that worked out:** I searched for these transfers just before creating them and found none. But all three create calls came back with a \"duplicate request ID\" error, pointing to transfers made a second or two later. My best guess is that each call ran twice during approval: the first created the transfer and the second was blocked by Airwallex's protection against repeat payments. I didn't retry anything. Instead I looked up each transfer and confirmed it has the right payee, amount and reference, and that there's only one per contractor. No one was paid twice."
  },
  {
   "end": "done",
   "summary": "003 | 1be49ae3-47d0-4a5a-b7fb-4ebb2ca9fe07 |\n\n- **Bank details:** all three saved payees match the sheet (account endings and sort code 04-00-04), so I didn't hold anyone back.\n- **No double payments:** before paying, I checked that nothing had already been sent for this payroll run. Each transfer has its own request_id (e.g. `BENCHDO744162-20261231-ada`), so if one is retried, Airwallex won't create a second payment.\n- **Pay date:** the transfer tool has no setting for a payment date, so I couldn't set 2026-12-31 myself. Please confirm in Airwallex that these will go out on the date you want."
  }
